{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-check5.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 25 pushed the confirmed recovery finding to its applied-state consequence with a new artifact on the same unit.\\n\\nWhy this step. The three confirmed properties for claim C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector had shown the disagreement in committed records: the resolution ignores a reply reporting the instance COMMITTED, the accept round nevertheless completes, the recoverer commits a NOOP vector, and after the Commit broadcast the already-committed replica keeps PUT while the recoverer and a third replica hold NOOP. What remained was whether that disagreement reaches the state machines, which was the last limitation named in the review.\\n\\nWhat was added. The harness now applies each replica's committed instance through the real executor (Exec.executeCommand, with r.exec set as production does) and reads each replica's state for the instance's key through state.Command.Execute, then emits a canonical applied_state_divergence event with the three values and an applied_match flag. The plan adds a fourth monitor and property on that event, sharing the instance identity and the committed_reply admission alias, with grounding in the executor, the state application and handleCommit. The local construction run gives peer_value 04 against recoverer_value and third_value (void), i.e. applied_match false: replica 1 applied the PUT and the other two applied nothing, so the divergence is now observable in applied state rather than only in records. One new uncertainty records that the harness invokes executeCommand directly rather than the production executeCommands loop, so scheduling, watermarks and the recovery timeout are not exercised.\\n\\nState. Audit spec version 6; both confirmed claims (C1 recovery, C2 durable record) and their reviewed checks are untouched; the accept-status candidate stays paused with its resume conditions; the formal outcome of this artifact awaits the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review. No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
